Root cause and correction for the Windows CEF activation failure. set_extension_enabled restarts the active Host set. During a requested stop, the exit monitor may reap a generation after the OS confirms termination but before stop_hosts_with_mode updates RuntimeHosts. The targeted single-host path already treated an absent matching generation as a confirmed stop; RuntimeHosts::remove_stopped did not, so the bulk restart interpreted a correctly reaped Host as a failure and returned extensions_host_unavailable. Windows scheduling made this race reproducible. The fix centralizes the rule in remove_stopped: only an OS-confirmed stop succeeds, and success includes a generation already absent from both bound and retained channels. Unconfirmed termination remains fail-closed. The targeted path now uses the same authority. Validation: 22 RuntimeHosts tests passed; 8 RuntimeLifecycle tests passed with 1 intentionally ignored prepared-runtime test; the ignored prepared monitored-restart test passed when invoked exactly; cargo clippy --all-targets --features windows-tests -- -D warnings passed; cargo fmt --check and git diff --check passed. Graphify update was invoked after the code change.
